Analyze source files for composition, modularity, and robustness breaks

Usage: vampiro check [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -p, --path <PATH>
          Path(s) to Rust source file(s) or directories to scan

      --target <TARGET>
          Explicit target revision (commit SHA or ref) for diff scope

      --base <BASE>
          Base revision (commit SHA or ref) for diff scope

      --full
          Scan all files (full scope) instead of diff

      --mode <MODE>
          Scan mode: guidance, tiered, or gate

          Defaults to gate (fail-closed). Advisory modes are dated downgrades: they require --advisory-until with a future ISO date, else the scan fails (vampiro-b7g advisory-lease TTL).

          [default: gate]

      --advisory-until <DATE>
          Advisory lease expiry (ISO YYYY-MM-DD) for tiered/guidance modes. Required for advisory modes; an expired/missing lease fails closed — renew by pushing the date forward (a visible, reviewable diff)

      --severity-threshold <SEVERITY_THRESHOLD>
          Severity threshold for gate mode (low, medium, high)

  -j, --json
          Output findings as JSON

      --sarif
          Output findings as SARIF 2.1.0

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
